@* Every page but the landing page renders inside the docs shell (Layout/DocsLayout.razor); the
   landing page and the not-found page opt out with @layout MainLayout. After a navigation the
   page's own H1 takes focus, so a screen reader starts reading at the new page. *@
@inject NavigationManager Nav
@implements IDisposable

<Router AppAssembly="typeof(Program).Assembly" NotFoundPage="typeof(Pages.NotFound)">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(Layout.DocsLayout)" />
        @* Not on arrival: <FocusOnNavigate> also fires on its first render, which here is the
           moment the app turns interactive - seconds after the page appeared - and it would pull
           focus away from wherever the reader had already tabbed to, the skip link included. It
           joins the tree with the first navigation, and its first render then is that one. *@
        @if (_navigated)
        {
            <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="routeData" Selector="h1" />
        }
    </Found>
</Router>

@* One host renders every tour the application starts, wherever it is started from - the part of
   this file every application needs. It sits beside the router rather than inside a layout so a
   tour survives every navigation, including the ones a multi-page tour makes itself.

   No Theme is passed: a tour that leaves its own Theme unset is drawn with data-bonboarding-theme
   "system", which leaves the choice to the application's stylesheet - and this site's (demo.css)
   follows its own light/dark switch there. A tour that sets Light or Dark keeps it whichever theme
   the site is in, which is what the theming page demonstrates. *@
<BonboardingRoot />

@code {
    private bool _navigated;

    // Subscribed ahead of the router (a parent initializes before the children it renders), so the
    // flag is already set when the router renders the page the navigation asked for.
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Nav.LocationChanged += OnLocationChanged;

    private void OnLocationChanged(object? sender, LocationChangedEventArgs e) => _navigated = true;

    public void Dispose() => Nav.LocationChanged -= OnLocationChanged;
}
